1T20:11:30Z","git_url":"git://github.com/python/mypy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:python/mypy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy","homepage":"https://www.mypy-lang.org/","size":77161,"stargazers_count":20064,"watchers_count":20064,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":3065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"When a class implements `__setattr__`, mypy still reports properties as read-only.\r\n\r\nMinimum example:\r\n\r\n````\r\nclass Foo:\r\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\r\n        self._d = {'a': 1}\r\n\r\n    def __setattr__(self, name: str, value: Any) -> None:\r\n        if hasattr(self, '_d'):\r\n            self._d[name] = value\r\n        else:\r\n            super(self.__class__, self).__setattr__(name, value)\r\n\r\n    @property\r\n    def a(self) -> int:\r\n        return self._d['a']\r\n\r\nf = Foo()\r\nf.a = 2\r\n````\r\n\r\nThe error points to the last line in the above code: `error: Property \"a\" defined in \"Foo\" is read-only`.\r\n\r\nExpectation: Since `Foo` implements `__setattr__`, mypy should allow the attribute to be set, even though it overlaps with a class property.\r\n\r\nThere are no issues identified if the property `a` is removed, and I am using version 0.781.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/9160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"c